.TH KNOWLEDGE-DUMP 1 "September 2026" "Knowledge Dump 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
knowledge-dump \- open Knowledge Dump or manage portable Codex context
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B knowledge-dump
.br
.B knowledge-dump codex-storage
.RI { discover | collect | verify | restore-test | restore-default }
.RI [ path ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B knowledge-dump
opens the native Knowledge Dump desktop application. The Codex storage commands
discover, copy, checksum-verify, and restore selected portable Codex task data.
.SH CODEX STORAGE COMMANDS
.TP
.B discover
Inspect the effective Codex home and selected local collection.
.TP
.BI "collect [" COLLECTION_PATH "]"
Refresh the selected collection from the effective Codex home.
.TP
.BI "verify [" COLLECTION_PATH "]"
Verify every collection file against its manifest checksum.
.TP
.BI "restore-test [" DESTINATION_CODEX_HOME "]"
Restore into a new isolated Codex home without touching the active profile.
.TP
.BI "restore-default [" COLLECTION_PATH "]"
Restore a verified collection into a fresh effective Codex home. This command
refuses to overwrite or merge an existing destination.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CODEX_HOME
Overrides the Codex source or fresh restoration destination. The default is
.IR ~/.codex .
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME , " " XDG_DATA_HOME , " " XDG_CACHE_HOME , " " XDG_STATE_HOME
Select the standard per-user Knowledge Dump storage locations.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/knowledge-dump/codex-storage.json
Remembered local Codex collection preferences when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR codex (1)
